  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hu">Hu</ref> 2</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Þæt men faran on cryd æfter ðeofan. Gyf neod on handa stande, cyðe hit man ðam hundredesmen, ⁊ he syððan ðam teoðingmannum; ⁊ faran ealle forð, ðær him God wisige, þæt hi tocuman moton; do ðam ðeofe his riht, swa hit ær Eadmundes cwide wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">That men go without delay in pursuit of thieves. If the need is urgent, the chief official of the hundred shall be informed, and shall forthwith inform the chief officials of the tithings, and all shall go forth, as God shall direct them, until they succeed in coming upon the thief. He shall receive his deserts as has already been decreed by Edmund.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Si necesse sit in manibus, indicetur hominibus hundredi, et ipsi postea indicent (denuntient) hominibus decimarum; et eant omnes pariter, quo Deus concedet (anneurit), ut inuenire possint; et faciant furi rectum suum, sicut prius Eadmundi regis fuit institutum.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
